   "unmapped": [
    "Expected losses of accepting/rejecting are linear in known type features: [l_k^+, l_k^-] = phi_k^T Theta*, with ||theta||, ||phi_k|| <= U known",
    "Selective sampling: costs observed only for human-reviewed jobs; endogenous queueing-delayed feedback",
    "Human review queue with time-varying oblivious capacity; known service rates mu_k; types aggregated into G groups given to the algorithm",
    "Regret against a fluid LP benchmark with per-period capacity constraints"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In particular, we assume that each job comes with a $d$-dimensional feature vector $\\bphi_k \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$ associated with its type $k$. The expected loss of accepting a job, $\\ell_k^+ = \\expectsub{k}{C_t^+}$, and the expected loss of rejecting a job, $\\ell_k^- = \\expectsub{k}{-C_t^-}$, both satisfy a linear model such that $\\ell_k^+ = \\bphi_k^{\\trans}\\btheta^{\\star,+}$ and $\\ell_k^- = \\bphi_k^{\\trans}\\btheta^{\\star,-}$ with two fixed unknown vectors $\\btheta^{\\star,+},\\btheta^{\\star,-} \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$. This model also implies $c_k = \\bphi_k^{\\trans}\\bolds{c}^{\\star}$ with $\\bolds{c}^{\\star} = \\btheta^{\\star,+} - \\btheta^{\\star,-}$."
  }
